<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>

    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>

    <PackageId>PandaTech.FluentImporter</PackageId>
    <Authors>PandaTech</Authors>
    <Description>Fluent API for importing CSV and Excel (XLSX) data into .NET 8+ with customizable property mapping, validation, type conversion, and support for init-only properties. Handles headers normalization, regex validation, custom converters, and detailed error reporting.</Description>
    <PackageTags>csv;excel;xlsx;import;importer;fluent-api;csv-parser;excel-parser;csvhelper;closedxml;data-import;file-import;fluent;mapper;converter</PackageTags>

    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/PandaTechAM/be-lib-fluent-importer</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/PandaTechAM/be-lib-fluent-importer</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>

    <PackageIcon>Logo.jpg</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>

    <Version>6.1.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>Literal sample-cell text.

Added: WithExampleText declares the exact text a generated sample cell should carry, exposed as
IImportColumn.ExampleText. WithExample is typed to the destination property, so a column converted from text into a
collection could not carry a usable example: the value was rendered through Convert.ToString as its type name, and
marking such a column NotEmpty made the generated template fail its own parse on the blank cell. ExampleText wins
over WithExample and over the value read from a supplied example model.

Note: IImportColumn gained a member. It is a read-only metadata view produced by ImportRule&lt;T&gt;.Columns and is
not an extension point, so this affects only code that implements the interface itself.

Previous release notes follow.

6.0.0 — Template generation and reader hardening.

Added: ImportRule&lt;T&gt;.Columns exposes ordered column metadata via the new public IImportColumn; new declarative
rule methods Describe, WithExample, WithExpectedFormat, WithEnumSource, WithAllowedValues, WithAliases;
ImportRule&lt;T&gt;.BuildTemplate generates a two-sheet xlsx (fillable data sheet first, legend second) with styled and
frozen headers, sample rows, localizable legend captions and in-cell dropdowns sourced from the legend;
ReadXlsx(stream, sheetName) selects a worksheet by name; TryReadXlsx/TryReadCsv aggregate every cell error instead
of throwing on the first; new MissingColumnsException, DuplicateColumnException and SheetNotFoundException;
InvalidCellValueException now carries a structured ImportError.

Fixed: header cells are read positionally, so a blank or leading-blank header cell no longer shifts every column
silently; cells are stringified culture-invariantly, so decimals and dates no longer break under a non-invariant
server culture; required columns are validated up front instead of surfacing as a misleading row-2 cell error;
fully blank rows are skipped; enum conversion rejects undefined numeric values; duplicate headers and unsettable
properties throw typed ImportExceptions instead of raw ArgumentException/InvalidOperationException; constant and
computed columns no longer require a header to be present; header matching collapses inner whitespace runs.

Breaking: IPropertyRule (internal) is replaced by the public IImportColumn; the internal ReadFromType enum is
replaced by the public ImportValueSource; WriteValue and ReadFromModel now return the rule for chaining;
RuleFor throws immediately when the property does not exist on the model; an optional mapped column may now be
absent from the file instead of failing every row.</PackageReleaseNotes>

    <!-- Build quality -->
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>

    <!-- Source/symbols -->
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <ContinuousIntegrationBuild Condition="'$(CI)' == 'true'">true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>

    <!-- Analyzer behavior -->
    <RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>false</RunAnalyzersDuringBuild>
    <RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>true</RunAnalyzersDuringLiveAnalysis>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>false</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\Logo.jpg" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
    <None Include="..\..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="ClosedXML" Version="0.105.0"/>
    <PackageReference Include="CsvHelper" Version="33.1.0"/>
    <PackageReference Include="Pandatech.Analyzers" Version="[2.1.0]" PrivateAssets="all"/>
    <PackageReference Include="SonarAnalyzer.CSharp" Version="[10.28.0.143324]">
      <PrivateAssets>all</PrivateAssets>
      <IncludeAssets>runtime; build; native; contentfiles; analyzers; buildtransitive</IncludeAssets>
    </PackageReference>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
